      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1745, settler Martin Krum bought 800 acres that would become Hillsdale, giving the town its early roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillsdale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Revolutionary War, Henry Knox passed through North Hillsdale in 1776, hauling cannons to Boston.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillsdale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1799 chartered Columbia Turnpike cut through Hillsdale, linking the Massachusetts line to Hudson and ferrying wool, rye, and wheat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillsdale%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Roeliff Jansen Kill and the adjacent park, both named for the early settler, sit just south of Route 22 in Hillsdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
